Q: Dynamic dispatching of template functions? A: <p>Here is a proposal that &quot;converts&quot; an integer whose value is known at runtime into an integer that can be used as non-type template argument. It works starting with c++17 though since
it depends on <code>std::variant</code></p>
<p>The idea is to rely on a variant whose types hold compile time constants of type <code>std::integral_constant</code>. For instance,
one could have:</p>
<pre><code>int main (int argc, char** argv)
{
    std::variant &lt;
        std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,0&gt;,
        std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,1&gt;,
        std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,2&gt;
    &gt; v;

    v = std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,2&gt;{};
    std::visit ([](auto idx)  { A&lt;decltype(idx)::value&gt;::foo();  }, v);

    v = std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,1&gt;{};
    std::visit ([](auto idx)  { A&lt;decltype(idx)::value&gt;::foo();  }, v);
}
</code></pre>
<p>where we use <code>std::visit</code> on a variant whose underlying object may change at runtime. Note how the <code>idx</code> parameter
of the lambda provided to <code>std::visit</code> holds our compile time information in the <code>std::integral_constant</code> type.</p>
<p>We can encapsulate this idea in a class <code>Selector</code> that can be used as follows:</p>
<pre><code>int main (int argc, char** argv)
{
    int n = argc&gt;=2 ? std::atoi(argv[1]) : 0;

    // Define a Selector object that handles integers up to 4 
    // and initialized with a runtime value  
    Selector&lt;4&gt; s(n);

    // We can retrieve type information from 'decltype(idx)' and use it as a NTTP
    std::visit ([&amp;](auto idx)  {
        A&lt;decltype(idx)::value&gt;::foo();
    }, s.get());
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now, for the definition of <code>Selector</code>. First, it takes as non-type template parameter the maximum integer value
(we can set some default value):</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;int Nmax=10&gt;
class Selector;
</code></pre>
<p>Next, we need to define our variant type with <code>Nmax</code> types of <code>std::integral_constant</code>, from 0 to <code>Nmax</code>. We can use
some metaprogramming here:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;int Nmax=10&gt;
class Selector {

    // a little helper here
    template&lt;std::size_t...Is&gt;
    static auto buildtype (std::index_sequence&lt;Is...&gt;)
        -&gt; std::variant &lt;std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,Is&gt;...&gt;;

    // here is our variant type 
    using integers_variant = decltype (buildtype(std::make_index_sequence&lt;Nmax&gt;{}));

    // we declare an attribute of this variant type.
    integers_variant value_;

public:
    // we need a getter on our variant attribute (to be used while calling std::visit)
    auto get () const { return value_; }
};
</code></pre>
<p>Finally, we have to inialize the attribute at construction:</p>
<pre><code>Selector(int n) {
    if (n&gt;=Nmax) { throw std::runtime_error(&quot;bad value&quot;); }
    value_ = select&lt;Nmax&gt;(n);
}
</code></pre>
<p>where <code>select</code> is defined recursively as follows. Note how we have to still return something
(a <code>integer_variant</code> default object) when <code>N</code> is zero, in order to always return the same type as a result of <code>select</code>:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;std::size_t N, std::size_t Remaining=0&gt;
constexpr auto select (int n)  {
    if constexpr (N &gt; 0) {
        if (n==0)  {  return integers_variant {std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,0+Remaining&gt;{}};  }
        else       {  return select &lt;N-1,Remaining+1&gt; (n-1);  }
    }
    else  {  return integers_variant{};  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Here is a full example:</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;variant&gt;
#include &lt;iostream&gt;

template&lt;int Nmax=10&gt;
class Selector {

    template&lt;std::size_t...Is&gt;
    static auto buildtype (std::index_sequence&lt;Is...&gt;)
        -&gt; std::variant &lt;std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,Is&gt;...&gt;;

    using integers_variant = decltype (buildtype(std::make_index_sequence&lt;Nmax&gt;{}));

    integers_variant value_;

    template&lt;std::size_t N, std::size_t Remaining=0&gt;
    constexpr auto select (int n)  {
        if constexpr (N &gt; 0) {
            if (n==0)  {  return integers_variant {std::integral_constant&lt;std::size_t,0+Remaining&gt;{}};  }
            else       {  return select &lt;N-1,Remaining+1&gt; (n-1);  }
        }
        else  {  return integers_variant{};  }
    }

public:
    Selector(int n) {
        if (n&gt;=Nmax) { throw std::runtime_error(&quot;bad value&quot;); }
        value_ = select&lt;Nmax&gt;(n);
    }

    auto get () const { return value_; }
};

template&lt;int I&gt;
struct A {
    static void foo() {  std::cout &lt;&lt; I &lt;&lt; &quot;\n&quot;;  }
};

int main (int argc, char** argv)
{
    int n = argc&gt;=2 ? std::atoi(argv[1]) : 0;

    Selector&lt;4&gt; s(n);

    std::visit ([&amp;](auto idx)  {
        A&lt;decltype(idx)::value&gt;::foo();
    }, s.get());
}
</code></pre>
